# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr): AI.23 merged into integrate/phase-AI via PR #629 (merge
# commit 8750587b). Independently re-verified against integrate/phase-AI HEAD: the free
# function is_same_host_peer_receipt no longer exists in crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs
# at all; PreparedWrite::is_peer_receipt() (send/mod.rs:311-313) now delegates cleanly to
# the single has_authenticated_peer_provenance() classifier (send/mod.rs:570-574), which
# is also used directly at line 541 in place of the old is_same_host_peer_receipt call.
# The overlapping-predicate duplication this finding describes has been eliminated on
# integrate/phase-AI. Status remains "open" at the top level only because the s22/s23
# occurrences below are stale pre-merge-forward snapshots on branches that never
# themselves merged this fix forward -- not because the duplication persists on the
# current integration branch.

